  "pseudos": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "While the state's armed apparatus detained 8,268 souls in March—a 25% surge from February—the official narrative from its data observers blames the weather, conveniently ignoring how brutal policies have kept annual crossings at decades-long lows. This is not a seasonal fluctuation; it's the predictable outcome of a system designed to criminalize movement. The facts expose the hypocrisy: the crackdown intensifies, yet the political architects of this crisis remain paralyzed in deadlock over funding, proving the machinery of control operates independently of democratic accountability.",
      "source": {
