    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "Behind the dry statistics—8,268 detained in March, a 25% increase—lies a narrative deliberately obscured by official voices attributing it to warmer weather. This explanation serves to naturalize a political choice: the continued detention of those labeled as 'cross-border persons' by a system that has sealed off legal pathways. The simultaneous deadlock among legislators on funding reveals the true crisis: a state apparatus that expands its power to arrest while its political masters cannot even agree on how to sustain it, leaving the machinery of repression to run on autopilot.",
